
                 SRI International's TerraVision System


This is the full source tree for the TerraVision 3D terrain visualization
system developed by SRI International. TerraVision lets you browse massive
volumes of terrain and other data that can be streamed over the Web and
interacted with in real-time. It is the product of 10 years of development
effort and is now released as Open Source under the Mozilla license agreement
(see the LICENSE file in this distribution). The code should compile under
most versions of Unix as well as under Windows platforms.

Instructions on compiling TerraVision can be found in the INSTALL file in
this directory. They can also be found, along with documentation and sample
data, on the TerraVision website at:

  http://www.tvgeo.com/

e.g., GNU autoconf configure files are provided for compilation under Unix
platforms. The configue must be performed in a separate build directory,
i.e. not in the source directory. For example,

  cd TerraVision
  mkdir irix6.5
  cd irix6.5
  ../configure --enable-tracing

Microsoft Visual Studio workspace and project files are also provided
to ease compilation on Windows platforms. The main workspace (.dsw)
files can be found in the TerraVision/winbuild directory.

The directory and library structure of TerraVision is briefly
described below.

Core Libraries
  - TerraVision     The core terrain rendering routines
  - glt             A version-independent OpenGL abstraction layer
  - pthr            An abstraction layer for the threading model
  - tsm             The tsmApi tileset manager for reading/writing data
  - tvutils         A suite of tools ontop of the core TerraVision library
  - vrml2           A VRML97 scene graph and parsing library

User Interface Libraries
  - plugin          An interface to the Netscape plugin API
  - PluginTV        A simple TerraVision window with no menus
  - TclTV           A Tcl/Tk interface to TerraVision (the best interface)
  - XmTV            An X/Motif interface to TerraVision (discontinued)
  - libTogl         A layer for Tcl/Tk to access OpenGL
  - winbuild        Contains the ActiveX user interface

3rd Party Libraries
  - DIS             Routines for DIS simulations 
  - conversions     The SEDRIS Conversions API for geographic coord systems
  - ghttp           The GNOME http library for reading remote data
  - jpeg            The JPEG library
  - libgeotiff      The GeoTIFF library
  - libpng          The PNG library
  - libungif        The ungif library (writes uncompressed GIFs)
  - libxml          The XML parser for GNOME
  - nsprnew         The Netscape Portable Runtime (NSPR) library
  - tiff            The TIFF library
  - zlib            The libz compression library

Supplemental directories
  - bin             Directory where MSVC projects build their output
  - nsprwin         Precompiled NSPR distribution for Windows
  - tsmUtils        Suite of tools built on top of the tsmApi
  - winbuild        Contains the MSVC workspace and project files
  - docs            Contains the TerraVision user guide and other docs

Obsolete Libraries
  - GATS, etc, libGats, libGeo, libGeo_Core, libGeo_DiscClient,
    libIss, libList, libMagic, libSem, libThread, libTileSvc,
    libhs, nspr, libwww, thread, xpm


